<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Страница-1" id="db17VAmTjs1ejl2BNyZd">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="AIFl7s1aNzeYCnpLCxcw-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;UI Description&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The application is going to have a single window just like the Task Manager. That window will have several modes: Startup, Settings, Running.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Startup mode/window will present a user two buttons to switch modes: Run (to go to the Running mode) and Settings (to go to the Settings mode). When the Run button is clicked, a file dialog will appear to let a user to pick up a process. Once it&#39;s selected, the mode gets switched to the Running one. Similarly, pressing the Settings button will switch the mode to the Settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Settings mode will contain several configurations. It will be largely empty since the current stage of the project does not provide much configuration capabilities but it will let a user to set a custom backend program file path and a default process to examine.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Running mode will contain a bunch of UI components related to the metrics. Particularly, a bar for showing how much CPU resources are consumed and a stack panel representing a thread count.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is how mode switching works:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Startup -&amp;gt; Running&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Settings -&amp;gt; Startup&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Running -&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp; Startup&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Startup -&amp;gt; Settings&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Settings -&amp;gt; Running&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Running -&amp;gt; Settings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Or&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Startup&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;---&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Running&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; \&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;/&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Settings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Under the hood the applicatiom is going to incorporate the command system of the Shared project to implement the Running and Settings mode.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Go to the &#39;UIDrafts&#39; file to examine the design&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="840" width="720" x="40" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
